Substantive theories focus on finding what moves or appeals to people.
These theories suggest that people have certain needs and/or desires that are internalized in the course of their growth.
These theories deal with what causes certain people to want exactly the things they do, and what influences in their environment lead them to do or don’t do certain things.
Two popular content theories are Maslow's theory of demand hierarchy and Hertzberg's two-factor theory.
In general, two behaviors can loom when managers begin to lead their former colleagues. The one end of the spectrum is the attempt to remain "one of the boys" (or one of the girls).
This type of manager has trouble making unpopular decisions, carrying out disciplinary actions, making performance assessments, assigning responsibilities and making employees obligatory.
At the other end of the spectrum, you turn into an unrecognizable individual who has to do everything differently than the team has done it.
Ultimately, the team leader is responsible for the team's success and failure.
This behavior often leads to rifts between the leaders and the rest of the team.
Virtual teams are guided according to the same standards of excellence as conventional teams, but there are subtle differences.
Virtual team members often have the function of a point of contact for their immediate physical group.
They often have more autonomy than traditional team members, as their teams can meet in different time zones that may not be taken into account by the local leadership.
The presence of a true “invisible team” (Larson and LaFasto 1989, p. 109) is also a unique part of a virtual team.
"The "invisible team"" is the leadership team to which each of the members reports. The invisible team sets the standards for each member."
Why would an organisation undertake the time-consuming process of introducing a learning organization? One goal for the practical implementation of organizational learning concepts is innovation.
When all available resources are used effectively across all departments of an organization, creativity and ingenuity can emerge.
As a result, an organisation's collaborative work on overcoming an obstacle can lead to a new innovative process of addressing the customer's need.
Before an organization can be innovative, the leadership must develop a culture of innovation as well as shared knowledge and organizational learning.
Angel (2006) explains the continuum concept as a method to help organizations become more efficient.
Neurobiological data provide physical evidence for a theoretical approach to the study of cognition, thus limiting the field of research and making it much more accurate.
The correlation between brain pathology and behavior supports scientists in their research.
It has long been known that different types of brain damage, such as trauma, injuries and tumors, influence behavior and result in changes in some brain functions.
Emerging technologies enable us to see and explore certain brain structures and processes for the first time.
This provides us with a lot of information and material to build simulation models that help us to understand the processes in our mind.
Although AI is strongly associated with science fiction, it is an important branch of computer science that deals with behavior, learning and intelligent customization of machines.
AI research includes the manufacture of machines to automate tasks that require intelligent behavior.
Examples of this are controlling, setting up strategies and schedules, the ability to answer customer diagnoses and questions, as well as handwriting, voice and facial recognition.
Such things have become independent disciplines focused on finding solutions to real-life problems.
Today, the AI system is widely used in economics, medicine, engineering and the military and has also been built into numerous software applications for home computers and video games.
Excursions are an important component for every school class. Not infrequently, a teacher would like to take her students to places where a bus trip is out of the question.
Virtual excursions represent a technical solution. Students can view museum pieces from the classroom, visit an aquarium or admire beautiful works of art.
Sharing an excursion virtually is also a great way to reflect on a journey and share experiences with future classes.
For example, students at Bennet School in North Carolina design a website every year about their trip to the state's capital. The website is rebuilt every year, but the previous versions remain online and serve as a scrapbook.
Blogs can also help improve students' writing skills. While students often have sloppy grammar and spelling at the beginning of their blogging experience, that usually changes when there's an audience.
Since students are often a very critical audience, the blogg author makes an effort to improve his style of writing in order to avoid criticism.
Blogging “also forces students to learn more about the world around them”. The need to arouse the audience’s interest inspires students to write wisely and interesting (Toto, 2004).
Blogging is a tool that inspires cooperation and encourages students to continue learning well outside the traditional school day.
Appropriate use of blogs “can enable students to become more analytical and critical; through the active response to internet materials, students can define their positions in the context of the texts of others and present their own perspectives on specific topics” (Oravec, 2002).
Ottawa is Canada's enchanting bilingual capital and is characterized by a number of art galleries and museums that showcase Canada's past and present.
Further to the south are the Niagara Falls, and to the north the untouched beauty of nature spreads in Muskoka and beyond.
All of these things and more characterize Ontario as what is considered typically Canadian by outsiders.
Large areas further to the north are fairly thinly populated and some are almost uninhabited wilderness.
A population comparison that surprises many: There are more African-Americans living in the U.S. than Canada has citizens.
The East African islands are located in the Indian Ocean off the east coast of Africa.
Madagascar is by far the largest in terms of the animal world and its own continent.
Most of the smaller islands are independent nations or belonging to France and known as luxurious seaside resorts.
