Downhill sports such as skiing and snowboarding are popular sports in which you attach skis or a snowboard to your feet and down a slope over a snow-covered surface.
Skiing is a popular travel activity with many enthusiasts, occasionally also known as “ski runners”, who are planning their entire holiday around skiing in a certain place.
The idea of skiing is very old – cave paintings with depictions of skiers go back to 5000 BC!
The origins of ski downhill skiing as a sport date back to at least the 17th century and in 1861 the first recreational ski club in Australia was opened by Norwegians.
Ski hiking with backpack: This activity is also called ski touring or skiing.
It resembles alpine touring or mountaineering, but does not necessarily include it, as the latter are executed in steep terrain and require much firmer skis and boots.
