Europe is a relatively small continent, but it has numerous independent countries. Normally you would have to apply for multiple visas and go through several passport controls if you want to travel through several countries.
In this regard, however, the Schengen area functions a bit like a country.
As long as you stay in this zone, you can usually cross the boundaries without having to go through passport control again.
Correspondingly, you don’t have to apply for a visa individually for each of the Schengen member countries with a Schengen visa, saving time, money and bureaucracy.
There is no universal definition of which manufactured items are considered antiques. Some tax authorities define over 100-year-old goods as antiques.
The definition shows geographical deviations where the age limit may be lower in areas such as North America than in Europe.
Handmade products could be described as “antiquity” even though they are younger than similar mass-producing products.
