Severe weather is the collective term for any dangerous weather phenomenon with the potential to cause damage, severe social disturbances or the loss of human lives.
Severe weather can occur anywhere in the world and there are different types of it that depend on geography, topography and atmospheric conditions.
Strong winds, hail, excessive rainfall and wildfires are forms and effects of severe weather, as are thunderstorms, tornadoes, water pants and whirlwinds.
Regional and seasonal severe weather phenomena include blizzards, snowstorms, ice storms and dust storms.
Travellers are urgently warned to pay attention to any kind of severe weather affecting their area, as this can affect all travel plans.
