Other islands are Livingston Island and Deception, where the flooded caldera of a still-active volcano offers a spectacular natural harbor.
Ellsworthland is the region south of the peninsula, which is bordered by Lake Bellingshausen.
The mountains of the peninsula merge here into the plateau and then rise again to form the 360 km chain of the Ellsworth mountains, which is divided in two by the Minnesota Glacier.
