The Plitwitzer Seen National Park is heavily forested, there are mainly beeches, spruces and fir trees and it offers a mixture of alpine and Mediterranean vegetation.
Thanks to its numerous microclimates, various soils and alternating altitudes, it has a remarkably wide variety of plant societies.
The area is also home to an extremely wide variety of animal and bird species.
There are rare fauna such as European brown bears, wolves, eagles, owls, lynxes, wild cats and capercaillies, as well as many generally common species.
